# Render Environment Variables — Safe Mutation Protocol

The Render API `PUT /v1/services/{id}/env-vars` **replaces the entire set**. Sending only new keys will DELETE every existing key.

## Required Steps (no exceptions)

1. **GET first**: Always fetch the current env vars before mutating.
2. **Merge**: Add/update keys into the existing set.
3. **PUT the full set**: Send ALL keys (old + new) in one call.

```powershell
# 1. GET existing
$existing = Invoke-RestMethod -Uri "https://api.render.com/v1/services/$svcId/env-vars" -Headers $headers
$merged = @()
foreach ($v in $existing) { $merged += @{ key = $v.envVar.key; value = $v.envVar.value } }

# 2. Merge new keys (add or overwrite)
$merged += @{ key = "NEW_KEY"; value = "new_value" }

# 3. PUT full set
Invoke-RestMethod -Uri "https://api.render.com/v1/services/$svcId/env-vars" -Method PUT -Headers $headers -Body ($merged | ConvertTo-Json)
```

## Never Do

- `PUT` with only new keys (wipes everything else)
- `PUT` without a preceding `GET`
- Assume the API is additive — it is NOT

## After Every Mutation

Always `GET` and list all key names to confirm nothing was lost.
